{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>אף חבב עמים.</b> He also showed special love to the tribes; each and every one is called עם, for Benjamin alone was destined to be born when the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Jacob (Genesis 35), ״גּוֹי וּקְהַל גּוֹיִם יִהְיֶה מִמֶּךָּ״." "<b>כל קדשיו בידך.</b> The souls of the righteous are stored with Him, as it says (I Samuel 25), ״וְהָיְתָה נֶפֶשׁ אֲדֹנִי צְרוּרָה בִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים אֵת ה' אֱלֹהֵיךָ״ (Sifrei)." "<b>והם תכו לרגלך.</b> And they are worthy of this, for they were driven to the underside of the mountain beneath your feet at Sinai." "<b>תכו.</b> A pu'al form — they were driven under the soles of your feet." "<b>ישא מדברתיך.</b> They took upon themselves the yoke of Your Torah (Sifrei)." "<b>מדברתיך.</b> The mem in it is close to the root, as in (Numbers 7) ״וַיִּשְׁמַע אֶל הַקּוֹל מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָיו״, ״וָאֶשְׁמַע אֶת מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָי״ (Ezekiel 2) — like מִתְדַּבֵּר אֵלַי; so too this <b>מדברתיך</b> — that which you were speaking to make heard to me, to say to them; טי\"ש פורפרלירש בְּלַעַ\"ז. And Onkelos translated it as 'they journeyed according to your words,' and the mem in it is a particle of use, serving the sense of מִן. Another matter — <b>אף חבב עמים</b>: even at the time of the endearment of the nations of the world, when you showed the nations smiling faces and delivered Israel into their hand — <b>כל קדושיו בידך</b>: all their righteous and their good clung to you and did not depart from after you, and you guard them." "<b>והם תכו לרגלך.</b> They press together and gather under your shadow." "<b>ישא מדברתיך.</b> They receive your decrees and your laws with joy — and these are their words."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {5 "the la'az is Old French tu, and por/pur parler (or paroler), 'you to speak/parley'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:52.568975232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}